{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>These are the generations.</b> Like הקורות, in the sense of מה ילד יום (Proverbs 27:1). Similarly, אלה תולדות יעקב (Genesis 37:2)." "<b>A righteous man</b> in his deeds." "<b>Perfect.</b> In his heart. And תמים תאר — HaShem is from doubling forms, and it [i.e., the adjective] is תמים." "<b>And the meaning of בדורותיו:</b> in his generation, at the time of the flood, and in the generations that came after him, for he lived until Abraham was 58 years old. The sign is that Abraham our father was 58 years old when Noah died."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {2 "Text reads מפעלי הכפל, literally 'products of doubling'; rendered hyper-literally.", 3 "נ\"ח read as numerological notation for 58 (נ=50, ח=8)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:30.203184196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}